I was trying to play with the shell plugin. So I connected a pixhawk to my computer (available on `serial:///dev/ttyACM0`), and ran the following code, which is essentially a modified `takeoff_and_land.cpp` example ([gist here](https://gist.github.com/JonasVautherin/8172654cb0b1de3b9b9046032b4ddf8c)):

```cpp
#include <chrono>
#include <cstdint>
#include <mavsdk/mavsdk.h>
#include <mavsdk/plugins/shell/shell.h>
#include <iostream>
#include <thread>

