I am testing a program that will control multiple vehicles at once. For testing I have two drones connected: one real drone over a telemetry radio and a second, simulated drone using a Docker container. The drones have been assigned different system IDs, and when I look at mavsdk.systems() I see two systems. The documentation suggests that when you create a plugin (like Telemetry) for a system it will give you data just for that system. Similarly, if you register callbacks with a plugin that was created for a system, it should fire and provide data only for that system. This does not appear to be what happens. If I create one Telemetry object for each system, they both get all data from both drones. This means that both Telemetry objects show, for instance, battery levels that toggle back and forth between the values of the two drones.

I have traced through the code and it looks like the issue is related to some changes in mavsdk_impl.cpp in function:
void MavsdkImpl::receive_message(mavlink_message_t& message, Connection* connection) {}

Towards the end of this function there are some remnants of routing logic. It currently looks like this:
for (auto& system : _systems) {
        if (system.first == message.sysid) {
            // system.second->system_impl()->process_mavlink_message(message);
            mavlink_message_handler.process_message(message);
            break;
        }
}

The commented out line looks like the message would be routed only to a system that matches the sysid of the incoming message. The line that replaces this just shovels the message to a generic handler, which appears to call all registered callbacks regardless of the sysid of the system that registered them. This would seem to explain the behavior I am seeing.  It looks like commit ad2f80b by [julianoes](https://github.com/julianoes) on May 9, 2022 is responsible for this change but I don't see any explanation behind this decision.

Is this the intended behavior? If so it seems interacting with multiple systems through one MAVSDK-based program is not possible anymore. Any thoughts or insights would be appreciated.

